course: dictionary
lesson: 12019
title: Chipper: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning fits. «You're very chipper this morning!» Here chipper describes a person's mood, so it means cheerful and full of energy.
explain: Look at the words around it. «We went to the chipper for supper.» In Ireland and Scotland, a chipper is a chip shop, a takeaway that sells fish and chips. Test it: "We went to the cheerful for supper" makes no sense, so here chipper must mean the shop.
explain: «The gardener fed the branches into the wood chipper.» Branches go in and small chips come out. Here a chipper is a machine. It can be dangerous, so only grown-ups should use it.
fact: Chipper (informal adjective) means cheerful and lively.
fact: In Ireland and Scotland, «chipper» can mean a chip shop, a takeaway.
fact: A wood chipper is a machine that chops wood or branches into small chips.
fact: Informal means a word is used in relaxed, everyday talk, not in formal writing.
fact: When a word has several meanings, check the clues to pick the right one: who or what is it, and where?
exercise: «Dad was chipper at breakfast, humming and smiling.» What does chipper mean here? | A machine for chopping wood | Angry and loud | A shop that sells chips | *Cheerful and full of energy
exercise: «We bought our dinner at the chipper in Glasgow.» What is the chipper? | A cheerful person | A machine that chops wood | A happy song | *A chip shop, a takeaway
exercise: «The wood chipper roared as it chopped the branches.» What is a wood chipper? | *A machine that chops wood into small chips | A bouncy pet | A chip shop | Someone who is always cheerful
test: «The chipper children skipped to school, singing.» What does chipper mean here? | *Cheerful and lively | A machine for chopping wood | Tired and slow | A takeaway shop
test: «A wood chipper is dangerous, so who should use it?» | Anyone, with no care at all | Only the youngest child | Nobody, because it is a toy | *Only grown-ups
exam: Mum said, «The chipper is open, shall we go?» What does chipper most likely mean here? | Sleepy | *Chip shop | Machine | Cheerful
